# Client rules for the Search and Type Index Services (lws10-index) (YAML-LD, format 0.8.0).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: Type search, as a client uses it
comment: >-
  What a client's QUERY requests to the session's Type Search Service must satisfy. The session
  accepts only the baseline query format, application/lws-query+json, and answers any other
  with 415 and Accept-Query.
specification:
  - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/
entries:
  - id: "#client-query-content-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-query-content-type
    label: The client's search requests carry a Content-Type naming their query format
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    area: index
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/query-content-type-required
    observe:
      role: typeSearch
      method: QUERY
    expect:
      otherHeaders:
        - headerName: Content-Type
          present: true
    guidance: >-
      Send every QUERY with the Content-Type of its query format, such as
      application/lws-query+json.

  - id: "#client-query-baseline-after-415"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-query-baseline-after-415
    label: After a search format is refused with 415, the client's next search uses the baseline format
    comment: >-
      A client may try a richer query format first. A portable client does not rely on it:
      once the server refuses it, the next search falls back to the baseline every server
      supports.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-query
    traits: [Discovery]
    area: index
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/client-baseline-only
    observe:
      role: typeSearch
      method: QUERY
      after:
        role: typeSearch
        method: QUERY
        statusCode: 415
        sameTarget: true
    expect:
      contentType: application/lws-query+json
    guidance: >-
      When a search is refused with 415, retry it in application/lws-query+json, the baseline
      format every server accepts.

  - id: "#client-restart-after-refused-page"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-restart-after-refused-page
    label: After a page of search results is refused, the client restarts the search
    comment: >-
      A page link the server no longer recognises, or that expired, gets 404 or 410. Trials are
      the client's next request to the Type Search or Type Index Service after such a refusal.
      The task makes the session refuse the next page link once with 410.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/#type-search-errors
    traits: [Discovery]
    area: index
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-index/client-restart
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Search, and follow the results to their next page. The session will refuse that page
        once with 410, as if it had expired.
      arm: pageGone
    observe:
      role: [typeSearch, typeIndex, searchPage]
      after:
        role: searchPage
        statusCode: [404, 410]
    expect:
      role: [typeSearch, typeIndex]
    guidance: >-
      When a page link is refused with 404 or 410, start again: send the QUERY again, or request
      the type index again. Do not ask for further pages of the old result.
